<section class="content-section" id="at-a-glance">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>At a glance</h2>

        <p>wordsofplainness.org is a <strong>static-first site with a thin dynamic edge</strong>. Every page is pre-rendered by Eleventy (Nunjucks templates over Markdown and structured data) and served as plain HTML from Vercel's CDN. Heavy media lives separately on Cloudflare R2 behind its own subdomain. The few things that must be dynamic—sign-in, a personal discipleship journal, newsletter and contact forms—talk to a small Django REST API on PythonAnywhere, and a handful of Vercel serverless functions handle automation such as social notifications. There is no front-end framework, no database behind the pages themselves, and no tracking scripts: a visitor's browser loads the site's own HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript, one Google Fonts stylesheet, and audio from the media CDN.</p>

        <p>The interesting engineering is less in the stack than in what the build does with it: build-time cross-referencing between book chapters and the Articles of Interfaith Discipleship, narration audio that highlights the text as it is read, song lyrics synced line-by-line to the music, a citation apparatus with over a thousand scripture links, all generated from the site's own book map, and validation gates that refuse to ship data that fails its checks.</p>
    </div>
</section>

